A two-column animated presentation combines modeling and management. On the left, epidemiological scenarios, community information, building information, human behavior, and virus-specific parameters feed risk modeling and infection risk. Environmental models, indoor setpoints, occupancy activities, and operating schedules connect to thermal comfort and energy consumption; small plots illustrate trade-offs. On the right, a building model and an Internet of Things illustration sit above changing digital-twin views. A simulation-prediction block and a large-language-model block connect to a video of a person interacting with a humanoid robot. The panels change within a fixed full-frame diagram; this is a program overview, not a labeled performance comparison.
